# Logs
#
# `/logs`, ANCHORED. Vite's starter template ships this line as a bare `logs`, and a gitignore
# pattern with no slash in it matches a file or directory of that name at ANY depth — so it also
# swallowed `src/pages/logs/`, the whole Log & Report page. Nothing warned: the files never showed
# up as untracked (ignored files are not listed), `git status` reported a clean tree, and a machine
# that pulled the repo simply never received the directory while every other change arrived.
#
# The leading slash pins it to the project root, which is the only place a log directory would
# actually be written.
/logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

node_modules
# Anchored for the same reason as /logs above: `dist` unanchored would hide any source directory
# that happened to be called dist. Vite only ever writes the one at the root. node_modules stays
# unanchored on purpose — nested ones are real and all of them should be ignored.
/dist
/dist-ssr
*.local

# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?

# Playwright browser smoke tests (npm run test:smoke)
test-results/
playwright-report/
e2e/.auth/
